1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:02,787
In this lesson, you'll make
your first shape appear:

2
00:00:02,827 --> 00:00:06,467
a teal circle, right in the
middle of the game screen.

3
00:00:06,867 --> 00:00:08,687
The lesson starts with two blocks:

4
00:00:08,807 --> 00:00:11,347
when the game starts,
and define sprite player.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,140
A sprite needs a look.

6
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,580
Open the Looks category.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,760
Drag look like a circle
into define sprite player.

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,320
It snaps into place.

9
00:00:19,767 --> 00:00:21,527
The player now looks like a circle,

10
00:00:21,567 --> 00:00:24,007
but it only appears when
the game creates it.

11
00:00:24,207 --> 00:00:25,307
Open Program.

12
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,680
Drag create sprite player at x 160,

13
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,100
y 120 under when the game starts.

14
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,640
It fits right in.

15
00:00:32,967 --> 00:00:37,527
The game screen is 320
pixels wide and 240 tall.

16
00:00:37,847 --> 00:00:42,027
So x 160, y 120 is right in the middle.

17
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,500
Now press Run.

18
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,767
And there it is: your teal circle,

19
00:00:45,807 --> 00:00:47,187
in the middle of the screen.

20
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:49,127
Over here is the code.

21
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:52,087
This is the real DIV
code your blocks made:

22
00:00:52,227 --> 00:00:53,807
the player, with its circle,

23
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:57,467
and the line that
creates it at 160, 120.

24
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:58,767
Well done!

25
00:00:58,807 --> 00:01:02,007
In lesson two, you'll make your
circle move with the arrow keys.
